<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siconulf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 851</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Siconulf of Salerno</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siconulf was the first Prince of Salerno. Brother of the murdered Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicard-of-benevento">Sicard of Benevento</a>, he was proclaimed prince at Salerno in 839 and waged a decade-long civil war against Radelchis I. The partition of 849 confirmed him as ruler of the western half of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> south, including Salerno, Capua and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucania">Lucania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siconulf.jpg" alt="Siconulf" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siconulf_solidus_671842.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
